# SRG-APP-000334-WSR-000024  -  CAT II
# The web server must uniquely identify and authenticate source by
# organization, system, application, and/or individual for information
# transfer.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000334-WSR-000024
group:           V-279028
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-002205 CCI-000366
control_rev5:    AC-4 CM-6

contribution:    Splunk both identifies and authenticates the source of transferred data
                 from its own configuration: connection_host stamps each received event
                 with the sending system's address or resolved name, TLS with a required
                 client certificate authenticates the sender on the receiving port, the
                 forwarder presents its own certificate and validates the receiver, Splunk
                 Web serves over HTTPS, and no UDP input is accepted because a UDP input
                 has no connection to authenticate.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] connection_host in ip|dns
check:           inputs.conf [SSL] serverCert non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [SSL] sslPassword non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] requireClientCert in true|1, with [SSL] accepted as an equivalent placement and the stanza resolved against the stanzas that actually exist
check:           inputs.conf [udp://<remote server>:<port>] * absent
check:           inputs.conf [udp:<port>] * absent
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] useSSL in true|1
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslPassword non_empty
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslVerifyServerCert matches ^(1|true)$
check:           web.conf [settings] enableSplunkWebSSL matches ^(1|true)$
check:           web.conf [settings] serverCert non_empty
check:           web.conf [settings] privKeyPath non_empty
